    "reviewed_conclusions": [
      "Confirmed both live variants and actual UI bindings: ogryn_thumper_p1→ogryn_thumper_p1_m1 (Kickback Lorenz Mk V) and ogryn_thumper_p3→ogryn_thumper_p1_m3 (Thugshot Lorenz Mk VII); the category suffix is not treated as a Mark ID.",
      "Confirmed I–IV melee_power_level_modifier .30/.34/.38/.42 and active duration 3.5s override the wrapper fallback; each independent on_equip ProcBuff listens for on_shoot, checks the slot at event time and requires num_hit_units>=3, with no kill condition, cooldown, stacking, or persistent held-stat gate.",
      "Confirmed the P1 pellet route counts distinct damageable hit units once after the shot, despite 32 pellets; the P3 actual shoot_hit_scan route counts resolvable direct hits despite the card projectile label. The actual Bash/sweep routes are melee and do not trigger on_shoot; no unrelated charge, throw, or delayed projectile route is inferred.",
      "Confirmed damage for the triggering shot resolves before queued event processing and stat-cache refresh; the later melee power-level read receives the effect. A repeat refreshes the single 3.5s timer; switching to melee preserves it while the Thumper remains equipped, and unequipping removes the on_equip buff.",
      "Confirmed the melee modifier enters the melee PowerLevel consumer only. Under the stated neutral-other-modifiers premise, P_scaled=100 and IV .42 gives 142 melee power-level input; this is not a guaranteed 42% final HP-damage increase.",
      "Confirmed RAW hash 8bb6569b bilingual strings, four-tier formatter values and 3.5s reconstruction; English formatting preserves no space after the percentage placeholder and two spaces before the time value. The literal 3+ is not an extra kill or one-hit-kill condition.",
      "Confirmed image 131 receipt, public download/hash/dimensions and visual acceptance, plus both weapon reverse pages and shared association entries match the actual two bindings."
    ],
